   "text": "This is arginine vasopressin, the nonapeptide Cys\u2011Tyr\u2011Phe\u2011Gln\u2011Asn\u2011Cys\u2011Pro\u2011Arg\u2011Gly\u2011NH2 with a Cys1\u2013Cys6 disulfide bridge. I read the residues in that order from the drawing and took the wedge/hash bonds as L\u2011amino\u2011acid configurations at every \u03b1\u2011carbon. I then worked out each @/@@ from the neighbour order in the SMILES. The \"C\" labels in the drawing are the cysteine CH2 carbons next to the S\u2013S bond.\n\n- Ring: Cys1 (free NH2) \u2013 Tyr (4\u2011hydroxybenzyl) \u2013 Phe (benzyl) \u2013 Gln (CH2CH2CONH2) \u2013 Asn (CH2CONH2) \u2013 Cys6, closed through the disulfide.\n- Tail from Cys6: Pro, then Arg (guanidine side chain), then Gly\u2011NH2.\n\nSMILES: N[C@H]1CSSC[C@@H](C(=O)N2CCC[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCN=C(N)N)C(=O)NCC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccccc2)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2ccc(O)cc2)NC1=O"
